Pushing HTML to GitHub Pages Locally via CMD

Install Git:
If you haven't already, download and install Git from https://git-scm.com/
Open Command Prompt:
Press Win + R, type cmd, and press Enter.
Navigate to your project folder:
Copycd path\to\your\project\folder

Initialize a Git repository (if not already done):
Copygit init

Create your HTML file:
Create an index.html file in your project folder.
Add the file to Git:
Copygit add index.html

Commit the changes:
Copygit commit -m "Adding my homepage"

Link to your GitHub repository:
Copygit remote add origin https://github.com/yourusername/yourusername.github.io.git
Replace yourusername with your actual GitHub username.
Push to GitHub:
Copygit push -u origin main
Note: If you're using an older Git version, you might need to use master instead of main.
Check your website:
Open a browser and go to https://yourusername.github.io

